__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local-only artifacts from the migration
source/
*.zip

# The rendered site lives on the gh-pages branch, which is force-pushed as a
# single orphan commit every run and so never accumulates. Versioning it here
# made docs/ 161 MB of a 197 MB repository, growing 12-20 MB per daily run,
# against 3.9 MB for all of data/, which is the actual product.
#
# docs/briefs is the exception and stays tracked. Those are the archive: written
# once, never regenerated, and the only thing under docs/ that cannot be rebuilt
# from a later run. The workflow restores the rest from gh-pages before the run,
# because docs/news and docs/prices are also the fetch cache.
#
# docs/* rather than docs/**, so the negations below can re-include: git cannot
# re-include a path whose parent directory is itself excluded.
docs/*
!docs/briefs/
!docs/.nojekyll

# The universe cache is resume state, not data. It is a 13 MB file that every
# daily run rewrites whole, and in git each rewrite stayed in history forever:
# 33 versions and 21.7 MB of the pack by 2026-09-13, adding about 70 MB a month.
# CI keeps it as the universe-cache release asset instead, replaced in place.
# Its fields are either recorded in the append-only panel under data/fundamentals/
# or recomputed every run, except op_margin_history and benford, which exist only
# here and in the published stocks-data.json.
state/stocks_universe.json
